Hexapod pipeline -- model and runtime provenance

quality_prepass.py
------------------
The GPU image installs MapAnything code from facebookresearch/map-anything commit
3d10cf7a3016fc0f9bb13a071ee66c47b10be0d9 (Apache-2.0). It loads only the approved
facebook/map-anything-apache weights, Hugging Face revision
00f9c245bbcb60522d1ed7f9e9d88462c6e3f38a (Apache-2.0).
https://github.com/facebookresearch/map-anything
https://huggingface.co/facebook/map-anything-apache

MoGe code is microsoft/MoGe commit 74fbce054ebed49800de42d0ad0e83495065719a
(MIT); its v2 module loads Ruicheng/moge-2-vitl-normal/model.pt, HF revision
cb0e8bbd6b1e243589717c78e750b1ba4c093acf (MIT).
https://github.com/microsoft/MoGe
https://huggingface.co/Ruicheng/moge-2-vitl-normal
The v2 geometry helper utils3d-moge uses upstream's exact code pin
62f09d58509485564e24d5d9f6aac9ee9ebc0c37 (MIT). Model packages are installed without
their optional viewers, training stacks or benchmark model dependencies.

quality_trainer.py
------------------
Our scale/shift depth alignment, depth-derived normal consistency, gradient residual
and axis-ratio hinge are independently implemented mathematics; no third-party loss
implementation is included. NumPy reference functions live in prior_maths.py.
The source-checked insertion seam operates on gsplat (Apache-2.0) commit
512d366b67073d77ca099ede742683c165dfc23b, version 1.6.0.
https://github.com/nerfstudio-project/gsplat

The GPU image also installs PPISP v1.2.1 (Apache-2.0), commit
df33809f7b3b20ac06de088dfc871b144b8fb54d:
https://github.com/nv-tlabs/ppisp
Fused-ssim and fused-bilagrid are pinned to the commits specified by that gsplat
revision's examples/requirements.txt; their upstream licences travel in the installed
packages. No upstream code is vendored into this directory.
